From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a webview's page asks the shell to open an app

A link for an application, such as zoommtg: or slack:, asks before it
launches. Chrome asks with ExternalProtocolDialog, a dialog anchored to
the outermost WebContents' window. For a <webview> guest that is the
shell's own window, so Chrome's unstyled "Open xdg-open?" dialog was
drawn over the desktop.

//chrome/browser/domicile sets an override that asks the guest's
element instead (domicile_external_apps.h). This patch carries the
parts in files Chromium owns:

- `external_protocol_handler.{h,cc}`: SetDialogOverride, run in place
  of the dialog before the outermost WebContents is taken, so the
  override sees the guest. Chrome's block list and remembered choices
  still decide whether to ask.
- Three lists, so that `DomicileExternalAppEvent`, the event a
  `<webview>` dispatches for the shell to answer, is compiled and
  reaches the page, as patch 0114 does for dialogs.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 .../external_protocol_handler.cc                 | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 .../external_protocol_handler.h                  | 11 +++++++++++
 .../renderer/bindings/generated_in_core.gni      |  2 ++
 .../blink/renderer/bindings/idl_in_core.gni      |  1 +
 third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/build.gni   |  2 ++
 5 files changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/external_protocol/external_protocol_handler.cc b/chrome/browser/external_protocol/external_protocol_handler.cc
index 289b835..69fbe69 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/external_protocol/external_protocol_handler.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/external_protocol/external_protocol_handler.cc
@@ -68,6 +68,9 @@ bool g_accept_requests = true;
 ExternalProtocolHandler::Delegate* g_external_protocol_handler_delegate =
     nullptr;
 
+// DOMICILE: see ExternalProtocolHandler::SetDialogOverride.
+ExternalProtocolHandler::DialogOverride g_dialog_override = nullptr;
+
 // Prefix for schemes that apps declare must not be launched by web content.
 // See crbug.com/539667062.
 constexpr std::string_view kLocalOnlySchemePrefix = "local+";
@@ -261,6 +264,14 @@ void OnDefaultSchemeClientWorkerFinished(
       return;
     }
 
+    // DOMICILE: see ExternalProtocolHandler::SetDialogOverride. Before the
+    // outermost WebContents is taken, so the override sees the guest.
+    if (g_dialog_override && !delegate) {
+      g_dialog_override(escaped_url, web_contents, initiating_origin,
+                        std::move(initiator_document));
+      return;
+    }
+
     // Anchor to the outermost WebContents, for e.g. embedded <webview>s.
     web_contents = web_contents->GetOutermostWebContents();
     CHECK(web_contents);
@@ -386,6 +397,11 @@ void ExternalProtocolHandler::SetDelegateForTesting(Delegate* delegate) {
   g_external_protocol_handler_delegate = delegate;
 }
 
+// static
+void ExternalProtocolHandler::SetDialogOverride(DialogOverride ask) {
+  g_dialog_override = ask;
+}
+
 bool ExternalProtocolHandler::MayRememberAllowDecisionsForThisOrigin(
     const url::Origin* initiating_origin) {
   return initiating_origin &&
